# One case carrying ONE no_error_log, used twice by the driver against two
# different -e paths. The pattern is deliberately one a healthy run never logs,
# so on the readable log the case passes on the MERITS -- which is what makes
# the unreadable-log run's verdict attributable to the log path and nothing
# else.
name    the worker did not die during this case
send    GET /__probe HTTP/1.1\r\n
send    Host: prober\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n
expect  status=200
no_error_log  worker process .* exited on signal
